---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
<div class="dc-section">
  <div class="dc-section__inner">
    <span class="dc-eyebrow-line" style="color:var(--accent)">Volunteered to hold a room? Read this.</span>
    <h1 style="margin:14px 0 0;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,44px);letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:var(--text-heading)">Facilitating a session</h1>
    <p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.5;max-width:64ch">You are not the expert. Your job is to keep the conversation moving, make room for quieter people, and make sure someone writes it down.</p>

    <div class="dc-grid dc-grid--3" style="margin-top:26px">
      <div class="dc-sticker-card">
        <span class="dc-sticker-card__step">FIRST 5 MINUTES</span>
        <h3>Read the card out.</h3>
        <p>Then go round: names, org, and one line on why they picked this room. Everyone speaks once, early on.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dc-sticker-card">
        <span class="dc-sticker-card__step">MIDDLE</span>
        <h3>Watch the edges.</h3>
        <p>If two people are running it, ask the room instead. "Has anyone had the opposite experience?" works nearly every time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dc-sticker-card">
        <span class="dc-sticker-card__step">LAST 5 MINUTES</span>
        <h3>Land it.</h3>
        <p>Three things we agreed, one we didn't, anything to try on Monday. Photograph the notes before you leave.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dc-quote-row">
        <p>If it goes quiet — let it. Ten seconds of silence usually gets you the best comment of the session.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="dc-section">
  <div class="dc-section__inner dc-prose" style="max-width:820px">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
</div>
